  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Virginia Buttula treated the service in her holiday homes as part of the product. She employed staff who could respond around the clock, unpack guests’ groceries and help arrange activities. Her approach combined well-equipped kitchens and carefully chosen furnishings with the aim of making visitors feel at home.\n\nAs a school-foundation chair, she described how community events supported scholarships. A new ladies’ lunch joined an established golf day and fathers’ lunch, raising money through sponsors, raffles and auctions. A separate annual appeal helped create an after-hours study area in the refurbished Seymour Library, giving students another place to work.",
    "html": "<p>Virginia Buttula treated the service in her holiday homes as part of the product. She employed staff who could respond around the clock, unpack guests’ groceries and help arrange activities. Her approach combined well-equipped kitchens and carefully chosen furnishings with the aim of making visitors feel at home.</p>\r\n<p>As a school-foundation chair, she described how community events supported scholarships. A new ladies’ lunch joined an established golf day and fathers’ lunch, raising money through sponsors, raffles and auctions. A separate annual appeal helped create an after-hours study area in the refurbished Seymour Library, giving students another place to work.</p>\r\n",
